      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T19:28:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need the `!is_new_avrcp_enabled()` check?\n\nThis basically says \"if AVRCP Target isn\u0027t enabled and AVRCP isn\u0027t connected,\" as `is_new_avrcp_enabled()` checks for the profile sysprop for AVRCP Target.\n\nDo you really want special logic for when AVRCP Target is disabled?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2867,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 2867,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "e3bc1c41518a06824aa43870709ef427d2464eca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "090daa1a_d3406e8a",
