      "writtenOn": "2024-03-29T16:44:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why check if the peer device is a source at all when AVRCP Target really only cares about sink devices?\n\nThe AVRCP Controller implementation can/should/already does it\u0027s own thing to help A2DP connect, as it leverages this btif_av state machine that you\u0027re dropping events onto.\n\nHave you tried:\n(1) Just check for the Sink SDP record of the remote device.\n(2) Don\u0027t alter the btif_av_sink_initiate_av_open_timer_timeout function\n\nI worry about altering the AVRCP Controller/A2DP Sink code path for concurrent source and sink devices like Android TVs and Cars. Scoping this down to deal with source devices only has a nice separation of responsibilities and keeps you from having to worry about what if the device you\u0027re connecting to is a source and a sink.",
      "parentUuid": "038d5d00_78e13fe3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4361,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 4365,
        "endChar": 3
      },
